# Backups
# `.env` and `.env.*` above do not cover `.env.bak-<stamp>`, and `kb install` writes
# `scripts/kb.py.bak-<epoch>` every time it runs. In `lacrx/assistant` a copy of `.env` made
# while editing it was swept into a commit by `git add -A` on 2026-11-11 and the blob is still
# in that history, which is why the ignore rule there is `*.bak` AND `*.bak-*` rather than
# just the first. Same two lines here, before the same thing happens.
*.bak
*.bak-*
